remediation:
1. Change logout endpoint to accept only POST requests (require state change):
   @app.route('/logout', methods=['POST'])

2. Enable CSRF protection in Flask-WTF configuration:
   app.config['WTF_CSRF_ENABLED'] = True

3. Add CSRF token requirement to logout endpoint with @csrf.protect decorator

4. Update frontend logout links to use POST with CSRF token:
   &lt;form method="POST" action="/logout"&gt;
       {{ csrf_token() }}
       &lt;button type="submit"&gt;Logout&lt;/button&gt;
   &lt;/form&gt;

5. Implement SameSite cookie attribute (Strict or Lax):
   SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE = 'Strict'

6. Apply CSRF protection to all state-changing endpoints (POST, PUT, DELETE)

7. Ensure HTTP-only and Secure flags are set on session cookies to prevent cross-site access
